l at Tirbin -\nBasar, West Siang District \n6.00 \n \n5.  Gujarat Construction of Synthetic Athletic Track at Naroda, \nDistrict Ahmadabad \n7.00 \n \n6.  Karnataka Laying of Synthetic Hockey Surface at Sainik School, \nBijapur \n5.50 \n \n7.  Laying of Synthetic Football turf at SAI Regional \nCentre,  Bengaluru  \n5.00 \n \n8.  Kerala Laying of Synthetic Athletic Track in Govt. Brennen \nCollege, Thalassery, Kannur  \n7.00 \n \n9.  Mizoram Laying of Synthetic Astro -Turf Football ground at \nLawngtlai Playground Lawngtlai. \n4.50 \n \n10.  Odisha Construction of Multi-purpose Indoor Hall in Kalinga \nStadium Sports Complex, Bhubaneswar \n8.00 \n \n11.  Puducherry Construction of Swimming pool  at Saradambal  \nNagar, Puducherry \n5.00 \n \n12.  Rajasthan Construction of Multipurpose Indoor Hall, Football \nGround and Athletic Track at LBS Government  Post \nG College Kotputli \n3.12 \n \n13.  Telangana Laying of Synthetic Athletic Track at Indira Gandhi \nOutdoor Stadium, Medak \n5.50 \n \n14.  Uttar Pradesh  Laying of Synthetic Hockey Field at Kailash Prakash \nStadium, Meerut  \n5.50 \n \n15.  Maharashtra Construction of Swimming Pool at SAI Western \nTraining Center, Aurangabad.  \n5.00 \n \n16.  Jharkhand Upgradation of Hockey and Football  Ground at SAI \nTraining Centre ,Hazaribagh.  \n2.07 \n \n17.  Uttarakhand Construction of Multipurpose Indoor Hall at Parade \nGround, Dehradun  \n8.00 \n \nTotal 95.19 \n \n \n\n \n \nList of infrastructure projects sanctioned under Khelo India Scheme in the year 2017-18 \nSl. No. Name of State Name of the Project Grant \nSanctioned \n(Rs. in \ncrore) \n1.  Andhra \nPradesh \nLaying of Astro Turf Hockey Field at District Sports Authority \nGround, Kakinada, East Godavari District. \n5.50 \n2.  Arunachal \nPradesh \nConstruction of Multipurpose Hall at Wakro under Lohit District. 8.00 \n3.  Construction of multi -purpose indoor hall at Khenewa under \nBamang Administrative Sub-Division East Kameng District. \n8.00 \n4.  Construction of multi -purpose indoor hall at TarakLangdi, Pania \nunder Kra-Daadi District. \n8.00 \n5.   Construction of multi -purpose indoor hall at Kiojoring, Nacho \nunder Upper Subansiri. \n8.00 \n6.  Assam Laying of Synthetic Athletic Track at SAI SAG centre ,Kokarj"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|1|STARRED   |472", "t": "Beautification of National Highways", "head": "O.I.H.\n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE,\n \nCOOPERATION\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK  SABHA\n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.\n \n472\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE \n25\nTH\n \nJUNE\n, 2019\n \n \nRASHTRIYA KRISHI VIKAS YOJANA\n \n \n472. SHRI RAMCHARAN BOHRA: \n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n   \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं\n\t\n\u0000कसान\n\t\nक\u0000याण\n\t\nमं\u0000ी\n \nbe pleased to state:\n \n \n(a) \n \nthe details of the criteria fixed by the Government for allocation of funds to various \nStates under the different ag\nriculture related schemes including Rashtriya Krishi Vikas \nYojana (National Agriculture Development Scheme) and National Food Security Mission; \n \n \n(b) \n \nwhether the Government proposes to formulate new parameters or amend the \ncurrent criteria for allocation \nof funds under the aforesaid schemes; \n \n \n(c) \n \nif so, the details thereof; \n \n \n(d) \n \nwhether the Government has received proposals from various States for allocation \nof additional financial assistance under the above said schemes; and \n \n \n(e) \n \nif\n \nso, the details thereof along with the action taken by the Government thereon?\n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n   \n(\nSHRI NARENDRA SINGH TOMAR\n)\n \n \n(a) \nto (c):   The criteria for allocation of funds to various\n \nStates under the different \nagriculture related schemes implemented  by the Government of India, including Rashtriya \nKrishi Vikas Yojana (National Agriculture Development Scheme) and National Food \nSecurity Mission, are given at \nAnnexure\n-\nI.\n \nGovernment   does not propose to formulate \nnew parameters or amend the existing criteria for allocation of funds under any of these \nschemes as of now. \n \n(d\n)\n \n& \n(\ne)\n:\n \nOn the basis of request\ns received from \nS\ntate\n \nGovernments and \non\n \nconsidering their performanc\ne and capacity to implement projects under various agriculture \nschemes, additional funds over and above the allocation has been provided to some of the \nStates from the funds available under these schemes during the financial year 2018\n-\n19 for \nimplementation\n \nof projects under the respective schemes.  The details of such additional \nallocation/ release made to States under some agriculture schemes during   2018\n-\n19 are \ngiven at \nAnnexure\n-\nII. \n \n \n\n \nAnnexure \n–\n \nI \n \nAnnexure referred to in reply to Lok Sabha Unstarred Qu\nestion No. 472 due for answer on \n25.06.2019 raised by SHRI RAMCHARAN BOHRA\n \n \nAllocation criteria of various agriculture scheme of Government India is given under:\n-\n \n \n \n1\n.\n \nRashtriya Krishi Vikas Yojana (RKVY) (Revamped as RKVY \n–\n \nRAFTAAR) \n \n \n \nSl.N.  \nCriteria/Parameters\n \nWeightage\n \ni\n.\n \nPercentage share of net un\n-\nirrigated area in a State to the \nnet un\n-\nirrigated area of all States.\n \n15%\n \nii\n.\n \nPercentage of small and marginal farmers in the state \ncompared to total number of small and marginal farmers \nin the \ncountry.\n \n20%\n \niii\n.\n \nMoving averages of the increase in plan expenditure in \nagriculture & allied sectors including animal husbandry, \nfisheries etc. in the previous 3 year period.\n \n30%\n \niv\n.\n \nAverage Gross State Value Added (GSVA) in agriculture \nand allied sectors in \nthe last 3 years.\n \n20%\n \nv\n.\n \nPercentage of youth population in the state compared to \ntotal youth in the country.\n \n5%\n \nvi\n.\n \nInverse of Yield gap between state average yield and \npotential yields as indicated in the frontline demonstration \ndata.\n \n10%\n \n \n2\n.\n \nNational Food \nSecurity Mission (NFSM)\n \n \nThe state\n-\nwise allocation under various components of NFSM i.e. Rice, Wheat, Pulses, \nCoarse Cereals and Nutri\n-\nCereals (Millets) \ni\ns calculated on the basi\ns of proportion of normal \narea, utilization of funds, release and performance \nmade during earlier years. NFSM being a \ncrop production oriented scheme, funds are released as per approved Annual Action Plan \n(AAP) in lump sum to the states and implementing agencies covered under the scheme. \n \n \nThe\n \nallocation criteria for NFSM (Oil seeds\n \nand Oil Palm)\n \nis base\nd on\n \nthe following criteria:\n-\n \n \ni\n.\n \nprevious years’ allocation of fund,\n \nii\n.\n \nAverage availability of fund to the states during the past three years,\n \niii\n.\n \nAverage fund utilized by the states during the past three years and\n \niv\n.\n \nPercentage share of state \nin area coverage and production of oilseeds during past \nthree years\n \n3\n.\n \nSub Mission on \nAgricultural Mechanization (SMAM) \n \n \n \ni\n.\n \n50% \nw\neightage to the \np\nroportion of states\n’\n \ncultivable area to total cultivable area of \nthe country  \n \nii\n.\n \n50% w\neightage to the \np\nroportion of \nstate area under small and marginal holdings to \ntotal area under small and marginal farmers in the country.  \n \n \n \n \n\n \n4\n.\n \nRainfed Area Development Programme\n \n \nState wise allocation is made based on performance of concerned state. Besides, State \nGovernment submits \nthe Annual Action Plan (AAP) and accordingly funds are released for \nimplementation"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|1|STARRED   |473", "t": "Execution of Projects by NHAI", "head": "�\n�\n������������������� �\n������������������������ �\n��\n��������� �\n���������������������� ���� �\n�\n� ����������������������� �� ����� ��