������������������\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n���������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n���������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�������� ������ ������ ��������� ����������� ���� ����������� ��� ������ ������� �������� ���� ������\n������ ����� ���� ����������� ��� ������ ������� ��������� ����� ����� �������� ��� ���������� �����������\n��������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�������������������������������������������������������������������������\n� �\n\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\nµ&KLOG\u00033URWHFWLRQ\u00036HUYLFHV¶�����������������������������������������������������������������������\n�������� ���������� ��������� ��� ��� �� ���������� ��� ���������� ���������� ��������� ����������� ������\n��������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n���������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������������\n���������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n���������� ��������� ��������� ���� ��������� ��� ��������� �������� �� ������"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|1|STARRED   |54", "t": "Damage by Cyclone Fani", "head": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ENVIRONMENT, FOREST AND CLIMATE CHANGE  \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 54 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 21.06.2019 \n \nMitigation of Greenhouse Effects \n \n54. SHRI NALIN KUMAR KATEEL: \n \nWill the Minister of ENVIRONMENT, FOREST AND CLIMATE CHANGE be pleased to \nstate: \n \n(a)  whether it is a fact that organic agriculture contributes to mitigating the greenhouse \neffect and global warming through its ability to sequester carbon in the soil; \n(b)  if so, the details thereof; \n(c)  whether a number of studies have revealed that soil organic carbon contents under \norganic farming are considerably higher and if so, the details thereof; \n(d)  whether the Government has taken any measures to work in collaboration with other \nministries to mitigate the greenhouse effect and global warming; and \n(e)  if so, the details thereof ? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER FOR ENVIRONMENT, FOREST AND CLIMATE CHANGE  \n(SHRI PRAKASH JAVADEKAR) \n \n(a) to (c) The government has launched the schemes of Paramparagat Krishi Vikas Yojana \n(PKVY) under National Mission for Sustainable Agriculture (NMSA) and Mission \nOrganic Value Chain Development for North Eastern Region (MOVCDNER) to \npromote organic farming to ensure long term soil fertility buildup, resource \nconservation and help in climate change adaptation and mitigation. The National \nHorticulture Mission was launched in 2005-06 as centrally sponsored scheme to \npromote holistic growth of the horticulture sector through area-based regionally \ndifferentiated strategies. The quantum of carbon sequestered due to this mission is \nestimated to be 137.72 MtCO2 from 2010 to 2016 (India’s Biennial Update Report \nsubmitted to United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change \n{UNFCCC}). \n(d) and (e) In order to mitigate the greenhouse effect and global warming, Government of \nIndia is implementing the National Action Plan on Climate Change (NAPCC) \nwhich comprises eight National Missions being implemented by different \nministries in specific areas of Solar Energy, Enhanced Energy Efficiency Energy \nEfficiency, Sustainable Habitat, Water, Sustaining the Himalayan Ecosystem, \nGreen India, Sustainable Agriculture and Strategic knowledge for Climate \nChange. \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|1|STARRED   |55", "t": "Promotion of Organic Farming", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE, \nCOOPERATION\n \n& FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK  SABHA\n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.\n \n55\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE \n  \n25\nTH\n \nJUNE, 2019\n \n \nPROMOTION OF ORGANIC FARMING\n \n \n*55. \n     \n \nSHRI HIBI EDEN: \n \n             \nDR. UMESH G. JADHAV: \n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS \nWELFARE\n \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n \nbe pleased to state\n:\n \n \n(a) \n \nwhether it is a fact that most of the farmers who are producing organic produce are \nstruggling due to poor policy measures, rising input costs and limited market and if so, the \ndetails of the measures taken by the Government to promote organic farming in t\nhe country; \n \n \n(b) \n \nwhether the Government has any special package for farmers who are doing organic \nfarming in the country and if so, the details thereof along with the steps taken by the \nGovernment to encourage organic farming in the country; \n \n \n(c) \n \nthe details of directions if any, to State Governments for encouraging organic farming \namong the rural farmers and awareness camps organised in this regard, State\n-\nwise \nincluding Karnataka; \n \n \n(d) \n \nwhether the Government has an effective mechanism to control\n \nthe balanced use of \npesticides/toxic chemicals in production of agricultural produce including fruits and \nvegetables and if so, the necessary steps taken by the Government in this regard; and\n \n \n(e)\n \nwhether the Government has decided to review the organic f\narming sector and if so, \nthe action plan of the Government in this regard?\n \nANSWER\n \nMINISTER OF AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n \n \n \n  \n(SHRI NARENDRA  SINGH TOMAR)\n \n \n \n(a) to (e\n):\n \nA statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n \n \n \n \n \n\n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (\ne\n) OF L\nOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.\n  \n55\n  \nDUE FOR REPLY ON \n25\nTH\n \nJUNE, 2019\n.\n \n \n \n(a) &\n \n(b):     \nThe Policy of Ministry of Agriculture on organic farming seeks to promote \ntechnically sound, economically viable, \nenvironmentally non\n-\ndegrading, and socially \nacceptable use of natural resources in favour of organic agriculture. It aims at sustaining soil \nfertility, conserving bio\n-\nresources, strengthening rural economy, promoting value addition, \naccelerating the growth\n \nof agro\n-\nbusiness and securing a fair standard of living for the \nfarmers and agricultural workers and their families.\n \n \n \n     \nBased on the policy directives, Government of India has been promoting Organic \nfarming in the states through dedicated schemes name\nly \nMission Organic Value Chain \nDevelopment North Eastern Region (MOVCDNER) and Paramparagat Krishi Vikas Yojana \n(PKVY) since 2015\n-\n16. Both the schemes aim at promotion of cluster/ Farmers Producer \nOrganisation (FPO) based chemical free, low input cost sust\nainable organic farming and \nsupport farmers from input procurement to market linkages.\n \n \n\n \nUnder PKVY,   assistance of RS 50,000 per hectare/ 3 years is allowed out of which \nRs. 31,000 (61%) is provided to farmer   directly through DBT   for input \n(biofertili\nsers, biopesticides, vermicompost, botanical extracts etc) production/ \nprocurement, creation of post harvest infrastructure,   marketing etc. \n \n\n \nUnder MOVCDNER ,\n \nassistance is provided to the farmers in a value chain mode \nstarting from formation of Farmers P\nroducer Organisations (FPOs), on/off farm input \nproduction, supply of seeds/ planting materials, post harvest infrastructure including \ncollection, sorting, grading facilities, establishment of integrated processing unit, \nrefrigerated transportation, pre\n-\nco\noling/ cold stores chamber, branding, labelling and \npackaging, etc .\n \n \nContd...2/\n-\n \n  \n\n-\n2\n-\n \n\n \nOrganic Farming has also been supported under other schemes viz Rashtriya Krishi \nVikas Yojana (RKVY) and Mission for Integrated Development of Horticulture \n(MIDH), \nNetwork Project on Organic Farming under ICAR. Third party certification of \norganic farming is promoted by Agriculture Processed Food and Export \nDevelopment Authority (APEDA), Ministry of Commerce.\n \n\n \nFarmers   adopt   low cost Participatory Guarantee System (PGS) of certification for \ndomestic markets under PKVY, where as \nthird party certified\n \norganic farming is \nencouraged under MOVCDNER for export of niche crops. \n \n\n \nThe major thrust of the Government has\n \nshifted from production orientation to \nmarketing linked production so that farmers can get better returns for their produce \nincluding organic produce. To further boost production of organic produce, a \ndedicated web portal\n-\n \nJaivikkheti.in\n-\n \nhas also been cr\neated to connect farmers \ninvolved in organic farming with consumers directly for better prices. \n \n(c):\n \nThe Department has been focusing on creating awareness and educating the farmers \nabout organic farming practices in the areas where clusters are formed. T\nhere is a provision \nof Rs. 80,000 per cluster financ"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|1|STARRED   |56", "t": "Kharif Crop Loss in Andhra Pradesh", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE, \nCOOPERATION\n \n& FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \n��������������������\n��\n����������������������������������������\n��\n����\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE \n  \n25\nTH\n \nJUNE, 2019\n \n��\n��\n��������������������������������������������������������������������\n��\n \n*56. \n    \nSHRI BALASHOWRY VALLABHANENI: \n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS \nWELFARE\n \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n \nbe pleased to state\n:\n \n \n(a) \n \nwhether Central Team visited Andhra Pradesh to assess the Kharif Crop loss in the \nState and if so, the details thereof; \n \n \n(b) \n \nwhether it is true that the State has put the loss at Rs. 1,869 crore in 13.6 lakh \nhectares; \n \n \n(c) \n \nif so, the details thereof; \n \n \n(d) \n \nwhether the State Government of Andhra Pradesh has requested the Union \nGovernment for exempting input subsidy for agriculture; and \n \n \n(e) \n \nif so, the action taken by the Union Government thereon?\n \n \n \n������������\n��\nMINISTER OF AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n \n \n \n  \n��������������������������������������������������������\n \n \n \n(a) to (e\n):\n \nA statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n \n \n��\n \n \n\n�������������������� ������������������ ������ ������ ������������ ������ ������������ �������� ������ ��\n��\n���� ������ ��\n������ ������������\n����������������������������������������\n��\n����\n����\n����������������������������������\n����\n����\n��\n��������������������\n��\n��\n \n(a) to (c): \n \nThe State Government of Andhra Pradesh declared drought in 09 districts \ncovering an area of 13.6 lakh hectare spread over 347 mandals during Kharif 2018 and \nsubmitted a Memorandum seeking financial assistance of Rs. 1466.91 crore from \nNational\n \nDisaster Response Fund (NDRF). An Inter\n-\nMinisterial Central Team (IMCT) \nvisited the drought affected areas of the State during 5\nth\n \nto 7\nth\n \nDecember, 2018. Based \non the findings of the IMCT and the recommendations of the Sub\n-\nCommittee of National \nExecutive \nCommittee (SC\n-\nNEC), the High Level Committee (HLC) in its meeting held on \n29.01.2019, approved an assistance of Rs.900.40 crore from NDRF.\n \n \n \n(d) & (e): \n \nNo, Sir. However, assistance towards \nagriculture \ninput subsidy is normally \nprovided to farmers as per S\ntate Disaster Response Fund (SDRF)/NDRF norms.\n \n*****\n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|1|STARRED   |57", "t": "Enrolment in Crop Insurance Schemes", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE, \nCOOPERATION\n \n& FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK  SABHA\n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.\n \n57\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE \n  \n25\nTH\n \nJUNE, 2019\n \n \nENROLMENT IN CROP INSURANCE SCHEMES\n \n \n*57. \n    \nSHRI T.N. PRATHAPAN: \n \n \nWill the Minister of \nAGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n    \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n \nbe pleased to state\n:\n \n \n(a) \n \nthe details of the number of farmers enrolled in the crop insurance scheme, Pradhan \nMantri Fasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY) as on date in various States including Kerala; \n \n \n(b) \n \nwhether the Government has decided to make Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana \nvoluntary\n \nfor the loanee farmer and if so, the reasons therefor; \n \n \n(c) \n \nthe steps taken by the Government to avoid fall in the enrolment of farmers under \nthe scheme; \n \n \n(d) \n \nwhether a margin (Premium minus compensation paid) of Rs. 15,975 crore was \nmade by insurance\n \ncompanies in the fiscal years of 2016\n-\n17 and 2017\n-\n18 under Pradhan \nMantri Fasal Bima Yojana across the country and if so, the details thereof;\n \n \n(e) \n \nwhether \n \nit \nis \ntrue that the current structure of the insurance scheme gives undue \nadvantage to the insurance companies to benefit from the State exchequer; and \n \n \n(f) \n \nif so, whether the Government is ready to control this and make PMFBY a purely \nfarmers’ welfare scheme?\n \n \nANSWER\n \nMINISTER OF AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n \n \n \n  \n(SHRI NARENDRA  SINGH TOMAR)\n \n \n \n(a) to (f\n):\n \nA statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n \n \n  \n\n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (\nf\n) OF L\nOK SABHA \nSTARRED \nQUESTION NO.\n \n57\n \nDUE FOR REPLY ON \n25\nTH\n \nJUNE, 2019\n.\n \n(a):\n \nState\n-\nwise details of farmer applicants enrolled during 2018\n-\n19 under Pradhan Mantri \nFasal Bima yojana (PMFBY) are given in \nAnnexure\n.\n \n(b):\n \nWith a view to provide financial support to farmers and to \nmake them eligible for next \ncrop at the time of crop loss due to natural calamities, pests & diseases,  the scheme is \nmade compulsory for the loanee farmers growing notified crops in notified areas and the \nscheme is voluntary for non\n-\nloanee farmers.  Howev\ner, requests/representations have been \nreceived from various quarters including farmer organizations, States etc. to make the \nscheme voluntary/optional for all farmers.  The revisions/improvements in the crop insurance \nschemes is a continuous process and d\necisions on suggestions/representations are taken \nfrom time to time after consultation with various stakeholders.\n \n(c):\n \nGovernment has taken several initiatives including active involvement of all \nstakeholders especially States and implementing insurance co\nmpanies for conduct of \npublicity campaign/awareness programmes including organization of camps in the rural \nareas to build farmer awareness about crop insurance schemes.    Insurance companies \nhave been asked to utilize 0.5% of gross premium collected by t\nhem for publicity and \nawareness generation.  Other activities for awareness generation involve the publicity of \nfeatures and benefits of the scheme through advertisements in leading National/local News \nPapers, telecast through audio\n-\nvisual media, distribut\nion of pamphlets in local languages, \nparticipation in agriculture fairs / mela / goshti, dissemination of SMS through Kisan \nPortal/national crop insurance portal and conduct of workshops/ trainings \n \nState officials, \nfinancial institutions and farmers. For \nnon\n-\nloanee farmers since crop insurance is optional, \nthe Common Service Centres (CSCs) \n \nand \n \nonline enrolment have been activated \n \nto provide \n \nContd…2/\n \n\n-\n2\n-\n \nthe services besides traditional modes like banks and insurance intermediaries.   Due to the \neffort\ns made by the Government coverage of non\n-\nloanee, for whom the coverage is \nvoluntary,  has increased from 5% under erstwhile schemes to 34%, which shows the \nacceptability of the scheme on voluntary basis.\n \nThough the coverage during 2\nnd\n \nyear of implementatio\nn of PMFBY was decreased \ndue to announcement of loan waiver schemes by some State and making Aadh\na\nar \ncompulsory for deduplication of coverage, but due to aforesaid efforts made by the \nGovernment coverage h\nas increased during 2018\n-\n19.   \n \n(d):\n \n \nNo, Sir.  In this regard, it is also informed that the difference between premium \ncollected and claims paid is not the margin for the companies.  The cost of reinsurance \nand administrative cost \no\nf gross premium also has to be borne by the Insurance \nCompani\nes.\n \n(e):     \n \nNo Sir. Selection of insurance company is made by the concerned State Government \nthrough competitive bidding process and the company quoting the lowest premium rate (L\n-\n1) \nis selected for implementation of the scheme.  Various checks and balan\nces for major \nstakeholders including insurance companies have been provided in the operational \n  \nguidelines of \n   \nthe sch"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|1|STARRED   |58", "t": "Sub-Mission on Agricultural Mechanisation", "head": "O.I.H. \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE, \nCOOPERATION\n \n& FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK  SABHA\n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.\n \n58\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE \n  \n25\nTH\n \nJUNE, 2019\n \n \n \nSUB\n-\nMISSION ON AGRICULTURAL MECHANISATION\n \n \n*58.\n    \nSHRI GOPAL CHINNAYA SHETTY: \n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS \nWELFARE\n \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n \nbe pleased to state\n:\n \n \n(a) \n \nwhether the People’s representatives Members of Parliament from Maharashtra had \nheld any discussion with the Minister of Agriculture and Farmers Welfare on Sub\n-\nMission \non agricultural mechanisation on 16th February, 2015; \n \n \n(b) \n \nif so, the details and the \noutcome thereof; \n \n \n(c) \n \nwhether the Government has taken any remedial steps in this regard; and \n \n \n(d) \n     \nif so, the details thereof?\n \n \nANSWER\n \nMINISTER OF AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n \n \n \n  \n(SHRI NARENDRA  SINGH TOMAR)\n \n \n \n(a) \nto (d\n):\n \nA statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n \n \n \n \n \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (\nd\n) OF L\nOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.\n \n58\n  \nDUE FOR REPLY ON \n25\nTH\n \nJUNE, 2019\n.\n \n \n(a) to (d):\n \n     \nOn 16\nth\n \nFebruary 2015\n, a meeting was proposed at Mumbai with Chief \nMinister , Minister of Agriculture, Members of Parliament of Vidharbha and Marathwada \nregion of Maharashtra regarding issues of farmers of the region. There is no record \nrelated to the above meeting available w\nith Government of India.\n \n \n       \n        \nAgricultural implements and machinery are essential inputs for modern \nagriculture. It enhances productivity besides reducing human drudgery and cost of \ncultivation. It also helps in improving utilization efficiency \nof other inputs.\n \n    \n \n \nTaking into consideration the above,\n \nto boost the farm mechanization in the \ncountry, a special dedicated scheme\n \n \nSub Mission on Agricultural Mechanization \n(SMAM) \nhas been introduced \n, under which subsidy is provided for purchase of v\narious \ntypes of \nAgricultural implements\n \nand machinery used for tillage, sowing, planting, \nharvesting, reaping, threshing, plant protection\n, inter cultivation and residue \nmanagement.\n \n \n        \n     \nFunds o\nf Rs.20.34,15.96\n, 15.00, 34.13 and 145.5 crore\n \nhave been released \nunder SMAM to Government of Maharasht\nra during the period of 2014\n-\n15, 2015\n-\n16\n, \n2016\n-\n17\n,\n \n2017\n-\n18 and 2018\n-\n19 respectively for distribution of \nagricultural machinery \nand equipment and establishment of Custom Hiring Centers. There\n \nis a con\nsiderable \nincrease in release of funds to the \nGovernment of Maharashtra\n.\n \n \n******\n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|1|STARRED   |59", "t": "Sub-categorisation of OBCs", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF INFORMATION AND BROADCASTING \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.59 \n(TO BE ANSWERED ON 21.06.2019) \n \nDOORDARSHAN KENDRAS \n59.  SHRIMATI RAMYA HARIDAS: \n         Will the Minister of INFORMATION AND BROADCASTING be pleased to state: \n(a) whether the Government is aware that many of the production centres of \nDoordarshan Kendras (DDK) have not produced any programmes for the telecast \nby Doordarshan and the equipment in its studio are lying idle and not generating \nany revenue for Government;  \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof;  \n \n(c) whether the Government has contemplated any plan including letting out the \nDDK studios to private production homes for generating adequate revenue and \nalso keeping the costly equipment in a working condition;  \n \n(d) if so, the details thereof; and  \n \n(e) if not, the reasons therefor? \n \n                                                               ANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF ENVIRONMENT, FOREST AND CLIMATE CHANGE; AND MINISTER \nOF INFORMATION AND BROADCASTING (SHRI PRAKASH JAVADEKAR) \n \n(a) & (b): Prasar Bharati has informed that Doordarshan has an extensive Network of \n7 National channels, 17 Regional Language Satellite Channels, 11  Channels from \nCapital Kendras.  There are 67 Kendras/Production centers spread across the \ncountry.  The manpower and Studios available in each Kendra/production center are \nbeing utilised optimally. \nAlmost all Kendras and Production centers are contributing programmes for DD \nChannels.  D ifferent formats of programmes like travelogue, documentaries, Short \nFilms, health shows, live-phone-in programmes etc. have been telecast on channels \nlike DD National, DD Kisan etc. \n(c) to (e): Technical facilities of Doordarshan  can be hired as per the Technical \nFacilities Rate Card which is already in place.  Doordarshan studios and equipments \ncan be hired by private  agencies as per the rate card available at \nhttps://doordarshan.gov.in. \n                                               *********************** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|1|STARRED   |6", "t": "POCSO Act", "head": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF INFORMATION AND BROADCASTING \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 6 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 21/06/2019  \n  \n \nBANNING OF TELECAST OF TV PROGRAMMES \n \n6.  SHRI ADHIR RANJAN CHOWDHURY: \n \n \nWill the Minister of INFORMATION & BROADCASTING   \n                            be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the telecast of any television programme has been banned by the \nGovernment recently;  \n(b) if so, the details thereof and the reasons therefor; and  \n(c) the steps being taken by the Government to establish a reasonable \nbalance between decency and freedom in the telecast of programmes in \nthe country? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF ENVIRONMENT, FOREST & CLIMATE CHANGE; AND \nMINISTER OF INFORMATION AND BROADCASTING  \n(SHRI PRAKASH JAVADEKAR) \n \n \n(a) to (c): All private satellite TV channels are required to adhere to the \nProgramme and Advertising Code as prescribed in the Cable Television Networks \n(Regulation) Act, 1995 and the Rules framed thereunder, as well as the Uplinking \nand Downlinking Guidelines 2011 issued by this Ministry. \n \n     Under the Cable Television Networks (Regulation) Act, 1995, the Central \nGovernment is empowered to prohibit transmission of a channel or a programme if \nit is considered necessary due to national security or in public interest or if it is \nfound to be in violation of Programme & Advertising Code. Similar mandate is \navailable under the Uplinking and Downlinking Guidelines, 2011, in respect of \nprivate satellite TV channels. \n \n     However, before taking a decision to prohibit any progr amme or a channel, the \nbroadcaster is given due opportunity to present his case as a matter of natural \njustice. \n \n****** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|1|STARRED   |60", "t": "Setting up of PSUs", "head": "���������� �\n������������������������� �\n���������������������������� �\n�\n���������������������������� �\n�\n������ ����������������������������� ��\n�\n�������������������������������������������������\n���������������������\n�\n���� �������� ���� ����������� ��������� ��� ���������� �������� ���� ����������\n������� ��� �������� ����������� ��� ���� ������ ��������� ������� ������ ��������\n�������������\n�\n���� ��������������������������������\n�\n���� ����������� ����� ��� ���� ����������� ��� ���������� ����� ������� ��� ����\n�����������������������������������������������������\n�\n�\n�������\n������ �\n���������������������������������������������������������������\n�������������������� �\n������������������������ ��\n�\n����� ��������������������������������������\n��\n����������� ��������������\n�\n������\n�\n�"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|1|STARRED   |61", "t": "Poor Performance of BSNL and MTNL", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE\nDEPARTMENT OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 61\nTO BE ANSWERED ON 21ST JUNE, 2019\nCHEAPER LAB TESTING FACILITIES IN HOSPITALS\n61. SHRI AJAY MISRA TENI:\nWill the Minister of HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE be pleased to state:\n(a) whether the Government proposes to implement any action plan with a view to provide\ntesting facilities at equal and affordable cost in Government and private pathology labs in orde r\nto provide low cost testing facility for various diseases in the country;\n(b) if so, the extent to which the people of the country are likely to be benefitted through it along\nwith the time by which this scheme is likely to be implemented; and\n(c) if not, the reasons therefor?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HEALTH AND\nFAMILY WELFARE\n(SHRI ASHWINI KUMAR CHOUBEY)\n(a):     Under National Health Mission (NHM), Government of India has launched National Free\ndiagnostic service initiative in 2015.This initiative aims to ensures the availability of 56\ndiagnostic tests at District hospital, 39 tests at Community Health Ce ntre, 19 tests at Primary\nHealth Centre and 7 tests at Sub-centre.\nThe guideline has a model tender document to engage the private provider’s labs for\ndelivering all high cost and technology demanding tests.\n(b):    The facility has already been rolled out. The services are being provided free of cost to all\nbeneficiaries from the level of Sub -centre up to the District Hospital level. The guideline has\nbeen launched in 2015 and disseminated to all States/UTs.\n(c ): Not applicable in view of (b).\n……………….."}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|1|STARRED   |62", "t": "Withdrawal of GSP by USA", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE\nDEPARTMENT OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.62\nTO BE ANSWERED ON 21ST JUNE,2019\nPRADHAN MANTRI SWASTHYA SURAKSHA YOJANA\n62. SHRI VINAYAK RAUT:\nWill the Minister of HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE be pleased to state:\n(a) whether implementation of Pradhan Mantri Swasthya Suraksha Yojana is being implemented\nin the State of Maharashtra;\n(b) if so, the details thereof;\n(c) the details of the funds rele ased for the projects under the said scheme in the State of\nMaharashtra so far; and\n(d) the up to date status of these projects?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HEALTH AND\nFAMILY WELFARE\n(SHRI ASHWINI KUMAR CHOUBEY)\n(a): Yes\n(b): Following projects have been undertaken by the Government under various phases of\nPradhan Mantri Swasthya Suraksha Yojana (PMSSY) in the State of Maharashtra:\ni. Setting up of new AIIMS in Nagpur (Phase-IV)\nii. Up-gradation of Government Medical Colleges:\n1. Grant Medical College, Mumbai (Phase-I).\n2. Government Medical College, Nagpur (Phase-II).\n3. Government Medical College, Aurangabad (Phase-III).\n4. Government Medical College, Latur (Phase-III).\n5. Government Medical College, Akola (Phase-III).\n6. Shri Vasantrao Naik Government Medical College, Yavatmal (Phase-III).\n(c): The details of funds released for the projects under PMSSY in the State of Maharashtra\nare given in Annexure.\n(d): The up to date status of the projects is given in Annexure.\n\nANNEXURE\nDetails of funds released and progress status in respect of the Projects in\nMaharashtra under PMSSY\nSr.\nNo.\nPhase Institute Approved Outlay Funds\nReleased\nfrom\nCentral\nShare\n(in Rs. Cr)\nProgress status as on date\n1 I Grant Medical\nCollege, Mumbai\nRs. 120 crore\n(Central share: Rs. 100cr;\nState share: Rs. 20cr)\n94.05 Completed.\n2 II Government\nMedical College,\nNagpur\nRs. 150 crore\n(Central share: Rs. 125cr;\nState share: Rs. 25cr)\n120.25 Completed.\n3 III Government\nMedical College,\nAurangabad\nRs. 150 crore\n(Central share: Rs. 120cr;\nState share: Rs. 30cr)\n98.12 Progress of Civil Work - 93%\n4 III Government\nMedical College,\nLatur\nRs. 150 crore\n(Central share: Rs. 120cr;\nState share: Rs. 30cr)\n94.72 Progress of Civil Work - 100%\n5 III Government\nMedical College,\nAkola\nRs. 150 crore\n(Central share: Rs. 120cr;\nState share: Rs. 30cr)\n86.34 Progress of Civil Work - 93%\n6 III Shri Vasantrao\nNaik Government\nMedical College,\nYavatmal\nRs. 150 crore\n(Central share: Rs. 120cr;\nState share: Rs. 30cr)\n101.28 Progress of Civil Work - 78%\n7 IV AIIMS, Nagpur Rs. 1577 crore 394.16  OPD Block & Residential\nComplex: Work in Progress\n(76%).\n Hospital and Academic\nCampus: Work in Progress\n(28%).\n MBBS Classes for 50 students\nstarted from the session 2018-\n19."}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|1|STARRED   |63", "t": "Share of Atomic Energy in Power Production", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF INFORMATION AND BROADCASTING \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 63 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 21/06/2019  \n  \nADVISORY TO TV CHANNEL \n \n63.  DR. SUBHASH RAMRAO BHAMRE: \nSHRI KULDEEP RAI SHARMA: \nSHRIMATI SUPRIYA SULE: \n \n \nWill the Minister of INFORMATION & BROADCASTING   \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a) the details of advisories issued by the Government to television channels during the \nlast three years;  \n(b) whether policy guidelines have been issued for uplinking of television channels from \nIndia, if so, the details thereof;  \n(c) whether his Ministry has issued any advisory regarding carrying of news and \ncurrent affairs content on TV channels recently, if so, the details thereof and the \nobjective behind the move; \n(d) whether all the TV channels are complying with the said advisories, if so, the details \nthereof and if not, the reasons therefor, and \n(e) the steps taken by the Government to ensure that all the TV channels comply with \nthe Government advisories? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF ENVIRONMENT, FOREST AND CLIMATE CHANGE; \nAND MINISTER OF INFORMATION AND BROADCASTING \n(SHRI PRAKASH JAVADEKAR) \n \n(a):     Issuing advisories as per law is a continuous process. This Ministry issues \nadvisories to private satellite TV channels from time to time for ensuring ad herence to \nthe Programme and Advertising Code as prescribed under the Cable Television \nNetworks (Regulation) Act, 1995 and the Rules framed thereunder. The Government \nhas issued 32 advisories in the past three years and the current year. Further, 34 \nadvisories had been issued between 2011 and 2014. \n \n(b):     Policy Guidelines for Uplinking Television Channels from India, notified in July, \n2000 were amended in December, 2011 and are available on Ministry’s website i.e. \nwww.mib.gov.in.  \n \n(c) to  (e): In accordance with the Uplinking Guidelines, 2011, an advisory dated \n22.05.2019 was issued by this Ministry advising all TV channels to carry programmes \nas mandated under the category of their permission viz. News and Current A ffairs and \nNon-News & Current Affairs.  \n \n All private satellite TV channels are required to adhere to the Guidelines and \nadvisories issued thereunder. Appropriate action i s taken whenever any \nviolation/contravention takes place. \n \n****** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|1|STARRED   |64", "t": "Transport Subsidy to Agricultural Exports", "head": "LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.64 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 21.06.2019 \n \nEMPLOYMENT GENERATED THROUGH TEXTILE SECTOR \n \n64. SHRI H. VASANTHAKUMAR: \n \nWill the Minister of TEXTILES वस्त्र मंरी \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a)   the estimated number of employment generated through textile sector in the country, State/UT-wise; \n \n(b)   whether the Government has launched any special scheme for creating more employment opportunities in \nthe textile sector and if so, the details thereof and the steps taken by the Government to pub licise the said scheme; \n \n(c)   whether Government has also proposed any special package to textile sector; and  \n \n(d)   if so, the details of the package thereof and the extent to which the handloom weavers are likely to be \nbenefitted State-wise including Tamil Nadu? \nउत्तर \nANSWER \nवस्त्र मंरी (श्रीमती स्मृतत ज़ूबिन इरानी) \nMINISTER OF TEXTILES \n(SMT. SMRITI ZUBIN IRANI) \n \n(a):   The Textile industry is one of the largest source  of employment generation in the country with over 45 million \npeople employed directly and another 6 crore people in allied sectors, including a large number of women and rural \npopulation. \n \n(b):   Government has lau nched several important sc hemes for employment generation and providing livelihood  in  \nhandloom, handicraft, powerloom for all the segments of the textile sector.  \ni. SAMARTH—Skill development and capacity building scheme.  \nii. Amended Technology Up -gradation Fund Scheme (ATUFS) for technology  upgradation of the textile industry , \npurpose being to attract investment and boost employment.  \niii. National Handloom Development Programme , Comprehensive Handloom Cluster Development Scheme, \nHandloom  Weaver Comprehensive Welfare Scheme and Yarn Supply Scheme s for promotion  of handloom \nsector and employment generation . \niv. Comprehensive Handicraft Cluster Development Scheme.  \nv. Power Tex India for powerloom weavers. \nvi. Silk Samagra—an integrated Scheme for development of silk industry.  \nvii. Integrated Wool Development Programme. \nviii. Scheme for Integrated Textile Parks.  \n \n(c) & (d): Yes, Scheme for Rebate of State and Central Taxes and Levies (RoSCTL) was recently approved by the \nGovernment to rebate all embedded state as well  as central taxes/levies up to 31 st March 2020 t o promote ease of doing \nbusiness and avoid procedural delays, rebate of taxes /levies  embedded in manufacturing . This applies to Made -Ups and \nApparels. \n \n The package is being implemented pan India and will benefit exporters including that of Tamil    Nadu. \n \n*** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|1|STARRED   |65", "t": "Commercial Coal Mining", "head": "5th Position \nGovernment of India \nMinistry of Coal \nLok Sabha \nStarred Question No. 65 \nTo be answered on 26.06.2019 \n  \nCommercial Coal Mining \n*65. SHRIMATI MEENAKASHI LEKHI: \nWill the Minister of COAL be pleased to state: \n(a) whether commercial coal mining is likely to help in reducing power tariffs \nand if so, the details thereof; and \n(b) whether regulatory measures are enforced to ensure that private players \nadhere to ethical norms while mining and if so, the details thereof? \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF PARLIAMENTARY AFFAIRS, COAL AND MINES \n(SHRI PRALHAD JOSHI) \n  \n(a) & (b): A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n  \n  \n\nStatement referred to in reply to parts (a) and (b) of Lok Sabha  Starred \nQuestion No. 65 for answer on 26.06.2019 asked by Shrimati \nMeenakashi Lekhi regarding Commercial Coal Mining. \n(a) : The policy for Auction of Coal Mines/Blocks for Sale of coal was issued \non 27.02.2018. The objective of the policy is to create a market place for coal \nwith multiple producers to drive competition and adopt best practices in \nmining as well as environment management. The auction of coal mines for \nsale of coal in a transparent manner is expected to encourage transparent \npricing of coal,  based on the market forces. Any variation in coal cost \ndirectly varies the energy charges.   \n(b) : Regulatory measures are enforced for everyone who does coal mining \nand are applicable for Government and Private Companies. In respect of \nsafety of workers engaged in coal mining, adequate guidelines/statutory \nprovisions have been made under the Mines Act, 1952 and the Mines Rules \n1955, Coal Mines Regulations, 2017 and Bye -laws and  Standing Order \nframed thereunder. The provisions of safety statutes are administered by the \nDirectorate General of Mines Safety (DGMS). DGMS also administers other \nallied legislations such as relevant parts of the Indian Electricity Act, 2003 \nand Central Electricity Authority Regulations, 2010.   \nFurther, as mandated under the Envir onment Impact Assessment \nNotification, 2006, under the Environment (Protection) Act, 1986, coal \nmining projects are required to undertake EIA studies which include impact \nof projects on surface/ground water, and prepare Environment Management \nPlan for obtaining environmental clearances. Project proposals are examined \nby the sectoral Expert Appraisal Committee (EAC) for their efficacy and \nadequacy and suitable conditions are imposed accordingly while granting \nenvironment clearances to coal mining projects. \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|1|STARRED   |66", "t": "Missing of AN-32 Aircraft", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF DEFENCE \nDEPARTMENT OF DEFENCE   \nLOK  SABHA \n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.66 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 26TH JUNE, 2019 \nMISSING OF AN-32 AIRCRAFT \n \n*66. SHRI ASADUDDIN OWAISI: \nSHRI BENNY BEHANAN:  \n \nWill the Minister of DEFENCE   j{kk ea=h \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether it is a fact that AN -32 aircraft went missing recently in Arunachal sector and \nif so, the details thereof and the reasons therefor along with  the number of persons including \ncrew members on board in the aircraft; \n \n(b)  whether the said aircraft has been traced and if so, the details thereof along with the \ndetails of special squads deployed/assigned for rescue and if not, the reasons therefor; \n \n(c)  whether it is a fact that AN -32 series of aircrafts are meeting with acci dents \nfrequently and if so, the details thereof along with the accidents occurred during the last four \nyears; \n \n(d)  whether the Government proposes to upgrade or phase out these aircrafts in a time -\nbound manner; \n \n(e)  if so, the details thereof along with the steps taken/being taken by the Government in \nthis regard; and \n \n(f) the number of aircrafts/choppers of Indian Air Force collapsed during the last four years? \n \n \n \nA    N    S    W    E    R \nMINISTER OF DEFENCE                                    (SHRI RAJNATH SINGH) \n      j{kk ea=h                  ¼Jh राजनाथ स िंह ) \n(a) to (f): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n*******  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRE D TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (f ) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 66 FOR ANSWER ON 26.06.2019 REGARDING \n‘MISSING OF AN-32 AIRCRAFT’.  \n \n(a)  AN-32 aircraft of IAF was reported missing in Arunachal Pradesh on 03.06.2019 \nwhen it was proceeding on a sortie to an Advanced Landing Ground at Mechuka. A total \nof 13 people included 06 crew members and 07 passengers were on board.  \n \n(b) The wreckage of the crashed aircraft was located by IAF helicopters on 11.6.2019 \nat a location of 16 km north of Lipo in Arunachal Pradesh. Aircraft and helicopters of \nIAF, Indian Army and Indian Navy were deployed for the search and rescue operations. \nIn addition, severa l teams comprising IAF and Army personnel as well as civilian \nmountaineers were tasked to locate the missing aircraft on ground and for rescue of the \ncrew and passengers. \n \n(c) AN-32 aircraft is the workhorse of the IAF transport fleet and has not met with \nfrequent accidents. In the last four years, in addition to the crash on 03.06.2019, only one \nAN-32 was lost on 22.7.2016 while flying over the Bay of Bengal.  \n \n(d) & (e): A part of the AN -32 fleet has been upgraded with better avionics and airframe \nreinforcement. The remaining aircraft are planned to be upgraded in a phased manner. \nThere is no plan to phase out AN-32 aircraft presently as they have useful residual life. \n \n(f) The number of aircraft accidents in the last four years  is given below: \n \nYear Fighter Helicopter Transporter Trainer \n2015-16 04 01 01 01 \n2016-17 06 02 - 01 \n2017-18 02 - - 03 \n2018-19 07 02 - 02 \n2019-20 (till \n20.6.2019 \n- - 01 - \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|1|STARRED   |67", "t": "Military and Sainik Schools", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \n  MINISTRY OF INFORMATION & BROADCASTING \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION No. 67 \n(TO BE ANSWERED ON 21.06.2019) \n \nNEW PRASAR BHARATI STATION \n67.  PROF. SAUGATA ROY: \nWill the MINISTER OF INFORMATION AND BROADCASTING be pleased to \nstate: \n(a) whether the Government has any proposal to set up new Prasar Bharati \nStations in the country;  \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof;  \n \n(c) whether the Government has taken note that some border areas in the country \nare still not been getting the coverage of Prasar Bharati; and  \n \n(d) if so, the details thereof and action taken to provide full coverage of DD/Prasar \nBharati? \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF ENVIRONMENT, FOREST AND CLIMATE CHANGE ; AND \nMINISTER OF INFORMATION AND BROADCASTING (SHRI PRAKASH JAVADEKAR) \n \n(a) & (b) Augmentation of coverage by All India Radio (AIR) and Doordarshan (DD) \nis an ongoing process  through installation of new stations/transmitters and \nexpansion of DTH services etc. in various parts of the country. \n \n(c) & (d) Doordarshan provides multi channel coverage through its free to air DTH \nservice in all the areas of the country including those located in Border areas. \n \nAIR covers the border areas through transmitters and alternative platforms such as \nDD Free Dish,  live streaming on mobile apps,  webcasting, podcasting through \nYoutube, Twitter, Instagram, Blog and OTT. \nGovernment of India has approved a special plan for strengthenin g of border area \ncoverage of AIR in Indo-Pak border in J&K and Indo-Nepal border.  \n        \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|1|STARRED   |68", "t": "One Rank One Pension", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF DEFENCE \nDEPARTMENT OF EX-SERVICEMEN WELFARE   \nLOK  SABHA \n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.68 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 26TH JUNE, 2019 \nONE RANK ONE PENSION \n \n \n*68. SHRI GOPAL CHINNAYA SHETTY:     \nWill the Minister of DEFENCE   j{kk ea=h \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a)  the present status of the implementation of One Rank One Pension (OROP) scheme; \n \n(b)  the details of the budgetary allocation, revised estimates as well as the actual \nexpenditure incurred for the implementation of OROP scheme during each of the last three \nyears and the current year ; \n \n(c)  whether there is some resentment among the ex -servicemen with the present model of \nthe scheme and if so, the details thereof; \n \n(d)  the details of steps taken for holding negotiation with them and steps taken/being \ntaken by the Government for redressing the issue; and \n \n(e)  the aim of setting up of Justice  Narasimha Reddy Commission for OROP along with \nthe main recommendations of the Commission and their implementation/status thereof; \n \n \n \n \n \nA    N    S    W    E    R \nMINISTER OF DEFENCE                                    (SHRI RAJNATH SINGH) \n      j{kk ea=h                  ¼Jh राजनाथ स िंह ) \n \n \n(a) to (e): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n******* \n \n\n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (e) OF LOK \nSABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. 68 FOR ANSWER ON 26.06.2019 \nREGARDING ONE RANK ONE PENSION \n \n \n \n(a)  The Government had issued orders on 07.11.2015 for implementation of One Rank One \nPension (OROP) with effect from 01.07.2014. \n \n(b)  A sum of Rs.10,795.40 crores has been released as arrears to Defence Forces \nPensioners/Family Pensioners on account of implementation of OROP.  Payment of arrears \non account of implementation of OROP order dated 07.11.2015 is made from Defence \nPension Budget Estimates.  Out of total Pension Budget, there is no separate \nallocation/budgeting towards OROP.  However, out of th e total Pension Budget, year -wise \ndetails of actual expenditure made on release of arrears of OROP are as under: \n \nFinancial year Amount disbursed on account of  \nOROP arrears \n2015-16 Rs.2,861.55 Crores \n2016-17 Rs.5,370.61 Crores \n2017-18 Rs.2,563.24 Crores \nTotal Rs.10,795.40 Crores \n \n(c) & (d) Some Ex-Servicemen Associations have been demanding  changes in methodology \nfor fixation of pension, periodicity of its revision etc. The Government appointed One \nMember Judicial Committee (OMJC) on OROP on 14.1 2.2015 to look into anomalies, if \nany, arising out of implementation of OROP. \n \n(e)  The Government appointed One Member Judicial Committee (OMJC) on OROP on \n14.12.2015 under Justice Narasimha Reddy to look into anomalies, if any, arising out of \nimplementation. The Committee was to take into account the financial impact of its \nrecommendations.  The Committee submitted its Report on 26.10.2016 .  An Internal \nCommittee has been constituted by the Government to examine the recommendations of \nOMJC with respect to feasibility and financial aspects.  The matter is under examination of \nthis internal Committee. \n \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|1|STARRED   |69", "t": "Construction of Railway Flyovers", "head": "----------- - - - - - - - ---------------------\nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF EARTH SCIENCES\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION No. 69\nTO BE ANSWERED ON FRIDAY JUNE 21, 2019\nCLEAN SEAS CAMPAIGN\n69. SRI G.M. SIDDESHWAR:\nWill the Minister of Earth Sciences be pleased to state:\n(a) whether the Ministry is proposing to join United Nations Clean\nSeas Campaign;\n(b) if so, the details of the observatory centres planned;\n(c) the steps taken by Government to control marine litter like\nplastics and microplastics?\nANSWER\nMINISTER FOR MINISTRY OF SCIENCE AND TECHNOLOGY AND\nMINISTRY OF EARTH SCIENCES\n(DR. HARSH VARDHAN)\n(a) Yes Sir.\n(b) As a part of this endeavour, it is proposed to monitor marine\ncoastal pollution at two locations, one each on the east and west\ncoasts of India.\n(c) A number of steps have been initiated by the Government of\nIndia, including monitoring, banning of single use of plastic bags,\ngenerating awareness among the public, school and college\nstudents and tourists of better recycling systems adopted for the\nmarine litter management. The data on source of marine litter for\nvarious beaches and coastlines being collected are provided to\nthe concerned ministries for taking appropriate measures.\nBesides, periodical awareness and cleanliness campaigns are\nbeing conducted in selected locations, in coordination with\nvarious national and international organizations to promote\nawareness among the public on the importance and the need to\npreserve our coasts.\n****\n"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|1|STARRED   |7", "t": "Malnutrition among Children", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE\nDEPARTMENT OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 7\nTO BE ANSWERED ON 21ST JUNE, 2019\nSHORTAGE OF DIALYSIS MACHINES\n7. SHRI MANSUKHBHAI DHANJIBHAI VASAVA:\nWill the Minister of HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE be pleased to state:\n(a) whether there is an acute shortage of dialysis machines as compared to their requirement in\nGujarat;\n(b) if so, the reaction of the Government in this regard;\n(c) whether the Government is providing any assistance at central level so as to increase number\nof dialysis machines in Gujarat; and\n(d) if so, the details thereof?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HEALTH AND\nFAMILY WELFARE\n(SHRI ASHWINI KUMAR CHOUBEY)\n(a) to (d):  Public Health is a State subject. Central Government provides support to the States\nthrough various interventions and programmes including National Health Mission. As informed\nby the State, there is no acute shortage of Dialysis Machines in the State.\nUnder National Health Mission, financial support is provided to all States/UTs for\nproviding the dialysis services. For Gujarat, as per State Programme Implementation Plans,\napprovals given are as below:\nFinancial Year Fund Approved (in lakhs Rs)\n2016-17 3178.31\n2017-18 2162.42\n2018-19 1102.00\n2019-20 1980.00\n……………."}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|1|STARRED   |70", "t": "Electrification of Non-Electrified Lines", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.70 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 26.06.2019 \n \nELECTRIFICATION OF NON-ELECTRIFIED LINES \n \n*70. SHRI N. K. PREMACHANDRAN:  \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the Government proposes to give priority for \nelectrification of non -electrified lines between two electrified lines \nand if so, the details thereof; \n \n(b) whether the Government proposes to electrify the Kollam -\nPunalur-Sengottai railway line mandatorily in view of its geographical \ncondition; \n \n(c) if so, the details thereof and the action taken thereon; and \n \n(d) the present status and proposed cost of electrification of Kollam -\nPunalur-Sengottai railway line? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS AND COMMERCE & INDUSTRY \n \n(SHRI PIYUSH GOYAL) \n \n \n \n(a) to (d) A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n\n***** \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) T O (d) OF \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.70 BY SHRI N. K. PREMACHANDRAN TO \nBE ANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 26.06.2019 REGARDING \nELECTRIFICATION OF NON-ELECTRIFIED LINES \n \n(a)   Yes, Sir.  In view the advantages of electrification and to \nachieve seamless train operation on electric traction over entire \nBroad Gauge network, Ministry of Railways has decided to \nelectrify balance Broad Gauge routes of Indian Railways.  \nAs against average 608 Route Kilometres (RKM)/year of \nelectrification done in the period 2009 -14, average 2,737 \nRKM/year was electrified in 2014 -19 period. It is planned to \nenhance this pace further. \n Action plan to e lectrify balance Broad Gauge routes is as \nunder:- \nYear RKM planned for \nelectrification \n2019-20 7,000 \n2020-21 10,500 \n2021-22 10,500 \n \n(b) Yes, Sir. \n \n(c) & (d) Present status for electrification of Kollam -Punalur-\nSengottai railway line is as under: \n\n(i) Electrification of Kollam -Punalur section has been \nsanctioned at a cost of `75.46 crore. Invitation of tender for \nelectrification work of this section is planned in July 2019.  \n(ii) Punalur-Sengottai section was converted to Broad \nGauge in 2018. Electrific ation of this section at a cost of `79.00 \ncrore is under sanction. \n \n****** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|1|STARRED   |71", "t": "Accreditation System for Legal Universities", "head": "����������������������������������������\n������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��\n������������������������\n����������������������������������������������������\n������������������������������������������������������������\n��\n��������������������������������������\n��\n������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��������������\n��\n���������� ���������������� �������� ���������������� �������� ���������������������� ���������������������������� ���������� ������������ ������ ���������������� ���������� ��������\n���������������� ������ �������� ���������� ���������� �������� �������� ������������ ���������������������� �������������� ������������ ������������ �������������������������� ������\n��������������������������������������������������������������������\n���������� ���������������� ������������ ���������� �������������������������� �������� �������������� �������������� ���������������� ������������ �������� �������������� �������� ��������\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n���������� ���������������������������������������������������