\n        Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Railways is considering the proposals to start a \nThiruvananthapuram-Velankanni- Madurai Train and a Main -line \nElectric Multiple Units (MEMU) service connecting \nThiruvananthapuram to Kollam, Nagercoil and Kanyakumari; \n \n (b) if so, the details thereof and the time by which the Mini stry \nproposes to execute these proposals; and  \n \n(c) if not, the reasons therefor? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS AND COMMERCE & INDUSTRY \n \n(SHRI PIYUSH  GOYAL) \n \n(a) to (c):  A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n***** \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (c) OF \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 258 BY DR. SHASHI THAROOR TO BE \nANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 10.07.2019 REGARDING TRAIN \nSERVICES \n \n(a) No, Sir.  \n(b) Does not arise. \n(c) Presently, Thiruvananthapuram is connected with Madurai by four \npairs of express and one pair of passenger trains While there is no \ndirect train service between Thiruvanan thapuram and Velankanni , a \nspecial train is being operated upto 28.07.2019 between Ernakulam \nand Velankanni. As far as connections between Thiruvananthapur am \nand Kollam are concerned, 62 pairs of train services are running \nbetween Kollam and Thiruvananthapuram/Kochuveli. Further, one pair \nof MEMU train viz. 66304/66305 Kollam -Kanniyakumari MEMU via \nThiruvananthapuram is being operated on the Kollam -\nThiruvananthapuram-Kanniyakumari sector in addition to existing \nMail/Express as well as passenger service operating on this sector. \nHowever, introduction of trains including MEMU service is an on -going \nprocess on Indian Railways subject to operational feasibility, traffic \ndemand, availability of resources etc. \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|1|UNSTARRED |259", "t": "Tribal Sub-Plan for Bihar", "head": "������������������� �\n���������������������������� �\n��������� �\n����������������������� ������\n��������