em\n \nVissannapeta\n \nA.Konduru\n \nVuyyuru\n \n--\n \nKrishna\n \nNuzvid\n \nBapulapadu\n \nAgiripalli\n \nPamarru\n \n--\n \nMalleswaram\n \n(H.Q) bantumilli\n \n--\n \nNandigama\n \n--\n \nJagaiahpet\n \n--\n \nMylavaram\n \nVelagaleru\n \nKanchikacherla\n \n--\n \nKalidindi\n \n--\n \nPedan\na\n \n--\n \nPenamaluru(H.Q.)\n \nKankipadu\n \n--\n \n7\n \nGuntur\n \nGuntur\n \nOld Market Yard\n \nTenali\n \nVemuru\n \nChilakaluripet\n \nNew Market Yard\n \nSattenapalli\n \nPiduguralla\n \nDachepalli\n \nGurajala\n \nRentachintala\n \nPonnur\n \nPedanandipadu\n \nKondapaturu\n \nK.B.Palem\n \nDugg\nirala\n \nNew Market Yard\n \nRepalle\n \nPonnapalli\n \nBhattiprolu\n \nGudavalli\n \nNarasaraopet\n \n \nBapatla\n \n \nVinukonda\n \n \nTadikonda\n \n \nKrosur\n \n \nMacherla\n \nDurgi\n \nRompicherla\n \n \nMangalagiri\n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \nIpur\n \nVellaturu\n \nGuntur\n \nKuchinapudi\n \nNizampatnam\n \nPhiran\ngipuram\n \n \nRajupalem\n \n \nVemuru\n \n8\n \nOngole\n \nOngole\n \nUppugundur\n \nTangutur \n \nKothapatnam\n \nKandukur\n \nVeerepalli\n \nMartur\n \n"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|1|UNSTARRED |521", "t": "Joint Action Plan against Global Terrorism", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n  \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 521 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 25TH JUNE, 2019/ ASHADHA 4, 1941 (SAKA) \n \nJOINT ACTION PLAN AGAINST GLOBAL TERRORISM \n \n521.  SHRI GOPAL CHINNAYA SHETTY: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Union Government has taken any steps or proposes to take steps \nto formulate a joint action plan to  check global terrorism affecting India,  Russia, \nUnited States of America and other countries; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; and \n \n(c) if not, the reasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI G. KISHAN REDDY) \n \n(a) to (b) :  The United Nations Global Counter Terrorism Strategy was adopted by \nthe Member States on 08.09.2006.  This Strategy is in the form of a resolution \nand has an annexed Action Plan.  The Global Counter Terrorism Forum (GCTF) \nserves as a mechanism for furthering the implementation of the UN Global \nCounter terrorism strategy and complements and reinforces existing multilateral \ncounter terrorism efforts.  India is one founding members of GCTF, which has 30 \nmembers, including United States of America and R ussia.  Besides, India has \nalso established Joint Working Groups on Counter Terrorism with 24 countries \nand with BIMSTEC, BRICS and EU.  Meetings of these Joint Working Groups are \nconvened from time to time to discuss counter terrorism issues and to share \nintelligence, experience, expertise, good practices and issues of mutual concern. \n(c): Does not arise. \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|1|UNSTARRED |522", "t": "FAME India Scheme", "head": "HEAVY INDUSTRIES AND PUBLIC ENTERPRISES \nDEPARMENT OF HEAVY INDUSTRY \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 522 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 25.06.2019 \n \nFAME India Scheme \n \n522. SHRI RAJESHBHAI CHUDASAMA:  \n \nWill the Minister of HEAVY  INDUSTRIES AND PUBLIC  ENTERPRISES be pleased \nto state: \n \n(a) whether the Government is  considering to further strengthen the FAME  India scheme \nfor the faster adoption of eco-friendly automobile technologies; \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n(c) whether vehicle length based  classification would target reduction in  vehicular \ncongestion and CO2 emission  based classification would align with the  overall vision of \ngreen mobility and reduction in Green House gas emissions; and \n(d) if so, the details thereof? \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF HEAVY INDUSTRIES & PUBLIC ENTERPRISES \n(SHRI ARVIND GANPAT SAWANT) \n \n(a) & (b): Based on outcome and experience gained during the Phase -I of Faster Adoption \nand Manufacturing of (Hybrid &) Electric Vehicles in India (FAME India) Scheme and \nafter having consultations with all stakeholders including Industry and Industry \nAssociations, Department of Heavy Industry finalized and accordingly notified the Phase -\nII of FAME India Scheme on 8 th March 2019, which is for a period of three years \ncommencing from 1st April, 2019 with a total budgetary support of Rs. 10,000 crore. This \nphase will mainly focus on supporting electrification of public & shared transportation, \nand aims to support through subsidies 7000 e -Buses, 5 lakh e -3 Wheelers, 55000 e -4 \nWheeler Passeng er Cars and 10 lakh e -2 Wheelers. In addition, creation of charging \ninfrastructure will be supported in selected cities and along major highways to address \nrange anxiety among users of electric vehicles. \n(c) & (d):Yes Sir, length based classification of ve hicles is applicable to decide GST on \nvehicles. Lower GST is applicable to smaller vehicles and higher GST rate is applicable to \nlarger vehicles with a view to reduction in vehicular congestion. \n Similarly, through CAFÉ norms, CO 2 emission is being regulat ed through which \ncompanies are being directed to reduce CO 2 emissions on each model manufactured by \nthem, to align with overall vision of Government in reduction of Green House gas \nemissions. \n \n***** \n\n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|1|UNSTARRED |523", "t": "Presence of IS", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n  \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 523 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 25TH JUNE, 2019/ ASHADHA 4, 1941 (SAKA) \n \nPRESENCE OF IS \n \n523.  SHRI KODIKUNNIL SURESH: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government is aware  of the presence of Islamic State (IS) in  \nvarious Indian States, especially in southern Kerala; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof and the action taken to check such activities; \n \n(c) whether the Government is further  aware of reports of Keralites being killed \nin US military action in Afghanistan, who  according to various media reports, \njoined IS and Taliban; and \n \n(d) if so, the details thereof and the reaction of the Government thereto? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI G. KISHAN REDDY) \n \n(a) to (b) :  Some instances of individuals from different States including Kerala \nhaving joined IS have come to the notice of Central and State Security \nAgencies.  The National Investigation Agency (NIA) and the States Police have \nregistered cases against IS members / sympathizers and have arrested 155 \naccused so far all over the country.  The Islamic State (IS)/ Islamic State of Iraq \nand Levant (ISIL)/ Islamic State  of Iraq and Syria (ISIS)/ Daesh has been notified \nas a Terrorist Organization and included in the First Schedule to the Unlawful \nActivities (Prevention) Act, 1967 by the Central Government.  IS is using various \ninternet based social media platforms to pro pagate its ideology.  Cyber space is \nbeing closely watched in this regard by the agencies concerned and action is \ntaken as per law.   \n(c) to (d): There is no confirmation of media reports to this effect. \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|1|UNSTARRED |524", "t": "Milk Production in Delhi", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF FISHERIES, ANIMAL HUSBANDRY AND DAIRYING  \nDEPARTMENT OF ANIMAL HUSBANDRY AND DAIRYING \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 524 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 25.06.2019 \n \nMILK PRODUCTION IN DELHI \n \n524. SHRI PARVESH SAHIB SINGH: \n \nWill the Minister of FISHERIES, ANIMAL HUSBANDRY AND DAIRYING मात्स्यिकी,पशुपालन और डेिरी मंत्री  \nbe pleased to state: \n  \n(a) the share of Delhi in the total annual milk production in India for the last five years: \n(b) whether Foot and Mouth Disease (FMD) and Brucellosis is negatively affecting milk producing ability \nin animals in Delhi and if so, the steps taken to control it; and \n(c) the steps being taken by the Government to boost animal husbandry and dairy industry in Delhi for \nenhanced milk producing capacity? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR FISHERIES, ANIMAL HUSBANDRY AND DAIRYING  \n(DR. SANJEEV KUMAR BALYAN) \n \n(a): The estimate of milk production is not reported by Delhi during recent past years. As per the estimates \navailable, the estimated milk production in respect of Delhi is 28 6.58 Million tonnes during 201 2-13 \nwhich is 0.2% of total milk production in the country in that year.  \n \n(b): As reported by the Government of NCT of Delhi, there is no negative effect on milk producing ability \nin animals in Delhi due to Foot and Mouth Disease (FMD) and Brucellosis. \n \n(c) The National Animal Disease Control Programme for Foot and Mouth Disease (FMD) and Brucellosis \nhas been approved by the Cabinet on 31.05.2019 as a new Central Sector Scheme with 100% financial \nsupport to carry out vaccination against Foot and Mouth Disease in entire cattle, buffalo, sheep, goat and \npig population and al so vaccination against Brucellosis in all the female cattle and buffalo calves (4 -8 \nmonths of age) once in a life time. Further,  Government of NCT of Delhi has also taken steps such as, ( i) \nBi-Annual vaccination against FMD carried out regularly , (ii) regular animal health services through \ndifferent Veterinary Hospital/Dispensary in Delhi and (ii) regular animal health checkup camps , for \nboosting animal husbandry sector in Delhi. \n \n \n***** \n"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|1|UNSTARRED |525", "t": "New KVK", "head": "भारत सरकार \nकृषि और ककसान कल् याण मंत्राऱय  \nकृषि अनुसंधान और शिक्षा षिभाग  \n \nऱोक सभा  \nअताराांककत प्रश् न सां. 525  \nददनांक 25.06.2019 \n \nनए कृषि षिज्ञान कें द्र  \n525. श्री अण् णासाब श कांकर लो‍ ऱ : \n \nक् या कृषि और ककसान कल् याण मंत्रय यब ातानक कक कृऩा करगेगक कक:  \n  \n(क) क् या सरकार कनाक क कक क्क् कोडी य क्षकत्र मगे नक कृषि षिञानान कक‍ र थ थाषऩत करनक ऩर \nषि्ार कर रबी बै;   \n(ख) यदद बां, तो तत् संांधय ‍ यौरा क् या बै; और  \n(ग)  यक कक‍ र का तक थ थाषऩत ककक एाकंगक? \n  \nउत् तर \n \nकृषि और ककसान क‍ याण तांरालाऱय तें रा‍ य तांराली \n(श्री कैऱाक चौधरी)   \n \n(क)  एय, नबीं। ाकऱगािय जएऱक मगे ऩबऱक सक बी दो कृषि षिञानान कगे र कायकरत बैं नामत:  \n \n(i)  भा॰कृ॰अ॰ऩ – कृषि षिञानान कगे र, ाकऱगािय-1  \nऩोथ :  तुक्कानाट् ी,  \nताऱुक : गोकक  \nजएऱा: ाकऱगािय-591224 \n{(मकएाान संगठन: ाकऱगांि इं ीग्रक कडी  रुरऱ डी किऱऩमगे  सोसाइ ी (ार्डकस)} \n \n(ii)  भा॰कृ॰अ॰ऩ – कृषि षिञानान कगे र, ाकऱगािय- 2  \nऩोथ : मट् ीकोप्ऩ,  \nताऱुक : ाैऱबोंगऱ   \nजएऱा: ाकऱगािय-591 147  \n{(मकएाान संगठन : कनाक क शऱंगायत कएुककिन सोसाइ ी, (कक कऱ ई)}  \n \nइस प्रकार, तुक्कानाट् ी गोकक ताऱुक, ाकऱगािय मगे कक गैर सरकारी संगठन द्िारा \nसबायता प्राप् त  कृषि षिञानान कगे र कक कायकक्षकत्र मगे क्क् कोडी य क्षकत्र िाशमऱ बै।   \n \n(ख) एिां (ग): उऩयुकक् त (क) कक उ्तरर कक मद्दकनरर प्र्न नबीं उठता।   \n \n******* \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|1|UNSTARRED |526", "t": "Threat of Islamic State", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n  \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 526 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 25TH JUNE, 2019/ ASHADHA 4, 1941 (SAKA) \n \nTHREAT OF ISLAMIC STATE \n \n526.  SHRI ANTO ANTONY: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has  issued notice to the State Government of  \nKerala and the UT Administration of  Lakshadweep regarding threat from \nIslamic State (IS) terrorists immediately after the attack in Sri Lanka; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof and the  steps taken by the Government in this  \nregard; \n \n(c) whether the Government intends  to enhance the security of coastal areas \nin view of the Sri Lankan attack; \n \n(d) if so, the action taken by the Government in this regard; \n \n(e) whether the Government has any  information regarding the number of \nIndians who joined IS; and \n \n(f) if so, the details thereof and the reaction of the Government thereto? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI G. KISHAN REDDY) \n \n(a) to (b) :  Intelligence inputs on terror threats are regularly shared with State \nGovernments / Agencies concerned with advice to take appropriate measures \nand sensitize their field formations to prevent any untoward incident. \n (c) to (d):  All Coastal States / UTs are advised regularly to enhance \nsurveillance and patrolling along the coastline, in view of the threat \nperception.  \n-2/… \n \n\n \n-2- \nLS.US.Q.NO.526 FOR 25.06.2019 \n(e) to (f): :  Some instances of individuals from different States having joined \nIS have come to the notice of Central and State Security Agencies.  The \nNational Investigation Agency (NIA) and the States Police have registered \ncases against IS members / sympathizers and have arrested 155  accused so \nfar all over the country.  The Islamic State (IS)/ Islamic State of Iraq and \nLevant (ISIL)/ Islamic State of Iraq and Syria (ISIS)/ Daesh has been notified as \na Terrorist Organization and included in the First Schedule to the Unlawful \nActivities (Prevention) Act, 1967 by the Central Government.  IS is using \nvarious internet based social media platforms to propagate its ideology.  \nCyber space is being closely watched in this regard by the agencies \nconcerned and action is taken as per law.   \n---x--- \n \n \n \n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|1|UNSTARRED |527", "t": "Setting up of NIPER", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF CHEMICALS & FERTILIZERS \nDEPARTMENT OF PHARMACEUTICALS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.527 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 25th June 2019 \n \nSetting up of NIPER \n \n527. SHRI MANOJ KOTAK: \n \nWill the Minister of CHEMICALS AND FERTILIZAERS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government proposes to set up National Institute of Pharmaceutical \nEducation and Research (NIPER) in the State of Maharashtra;  \n(b) if so, the details thereof;  \n(c) whether the Government is considering to open NIPER in various States keeping in \nview the huge potential in the form of human resources,; and  \n(d) if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER IN THE MINISTRY OF CHEMICALS AND FERTILIZERS \n(SHRI D. V. SADANANDA GOWDA)                                \n \n(a) and (b): Presently, seven National Institutes of Pharmaceutical Education and \nResearch (NIPERs) are functioning in various parts of the country. During the year \n2015-16, the Government did propose to set up three more NIPERs – one each in the \nStates of Maharashtra, Rajasthan and Chhattisgarh.  \n \n(c) and (d): The NITI Aayog, after conducting evaluation of the existing NIPERs, has \nrecommended for consolidation of the existing Institutes rather than setting up new \nNIPERs. Subsequently, the Expenditure Finance C ommittee (EFC) in its meeting held \non 26.03.2018 has also recommended for deferring the setting up of the proposed new \nNIPERs. As such, the Government is not proposing to open up any new NIPER at this \njuncture.  \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|1|UNSTARRED |528", "t": "Subsidized Foodgrains under NFSA", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF CONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD & PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION \nDEPARTMENT OF FOOD AND PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 528   \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 25th JUNE, 2019 \n \nSUBSIDIZED FOODGRAINS UNDER NFSA \n \n528.  SHRIMATI MEENAKASHI LEKHI:  \nSHRI SUMEDHANAND SARSWATI: \n \nWill the Minister of CONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD AND PUBLIC \nDISTRIBUTION उपभोक्ता त मल,ाखतद्ा औा तावर्ज�ाका्औता  मं be pleased to state: \n \n(a)   the details of the beneficiaries who receive highly subsidized \nfoodgrain under the National Food Security Act (NFSA);  \n \n(b)   whether the Government proposes to review the percentage of the \nbeneficiaries covered under National Food Security Scheme in the country \nagain;  \n \n(c)   if so, whether the Government proposes to increase the number and \npercentage of beneficiaries in the country including Rajasthan; and  \n \n(d)   if so, the details thereof?  \nA N S W E R \nMINISTER OF CONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD & PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION \n(SHRI RAMVILAS PASWAN) \n (a):  The National Food Security Act, 2013 (NFSA)  is being implemented in \nall the States/UTs, on an all India basis with a targeted coverage of 81.35 crore \npersons. The Act provides for coverage of upto 75% of the rural population and \n50% of the urban population to receive highly subsidized foodgrains. \nCorresponding to the all India coverage of 75% and 50% in the rural and urban \nareas respectively, State- wise coverage under NFSA was determined by the \nerstwhile Planning Commission (now NITI Aayog) using the population figures \nof 2011 Census and the National Sample Survey Household Consumption \nSurvey data for 2011-12. Section 9 of the Act, also provides that the coverage \nunder the Act is to be calculated on the basis of the population estimates as \nper the census of  which the relevant figures have been published. \nBeneficiaries under the Act are covered under two household categories viz. \nAntyodaya Anna Yojana (AAY) and priority households. Section 10 of the Act \nprovides that within the number of persons determined for coverage under \nthe Act, the State Government shall identify the households under AAY as \nper guidelines applicable to the said scheme and the remaining households \nas priority households to be covered under TPDS, in accordance with such \nguidelines as the State Government may specify. \n(b) to (d):  No proposal to revise the coverage under NFSA for any \nState/UT including Rajasthan is under consideration of the Government. \n**** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|1|UNSTARRED |529", "t": "R&D in FPI Sector", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF FOOD PROCESSING INDUSTRIES \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.529 \nANSWERED ON 25TH JUNE, 2019 \n  \nR & D IN FPI SECTOR  \n \n529. SHRI JAYADEV GALLA: \n                    \nWill the Minister of FOOD PROCESSING INDUSTRIES be pleased to state: \n  \n(a) the reasons that funds allocated for R&D in food processing sector has come down from \nRs.10.5 crore in 2012-13 to Rs.5.8 crore in 2016-17;  \n \n(b) the status of implementation of R&D in food processing sector since April, 2017 by the \nGovernment; and  \n \n(c) the details of targets set and achieved since 2017?  \n   \n \nANSWER \n \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR FOOD PROCESSING INDUSTRIES \n(SHRI RAMESWAR TELI) \n  \n(a): The budget allocations are done as per the requirement of funds for the new projects \nand to meet the outstanding liabilities of the projects already approved. The outstanding \nliabilities of projects approved by the Ministry before 2012 -13 declined in subsequent years \nand accordingly the budget allocation for the R&D Scheme also reduced. \n  \n(b) & (c): R&D Scheme is now a part of Human Resource & Institutions Scheme under the \numbrella scheme of the Ministry i.e. Pradhan Mantri Kisan SAMPADA Yojana (PMKSY). \nThe scheme is being implemented with an alloca tion of Rs.50 crores to meet the committed \nliability of on -going projects and taking up of 100 new projects till 2020. The Ministry has \napproved 35 new projects till the end of 2018-19 with approved grant-in-aid of Rs.14.75 crores. \n  \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|1|UNSTARRED |53", "t": "Domestic Violence on Children", "head": "������������������� �\n��������������������������������������� �\n��\n��������� �\n������������������������ �\n���������������������������� �\n�\n����������������������������� �\n���������������������������\n����������������������������������������������������������������������\n��������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�������������������������������������������\n������������������������������������������������������������������