HE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) FOR YOUTH \nAFFAIRS AND SPORTS \n(SHRI KIREN RIJIJU) \n \n(a) & (b)   The Ministry organizes the National Youth Festival every \nyear on the birth an niversary of Swami Vivekananda from 12th to 16th \nJanuary. The Hon ’ble Prime Minister shared the idea of youth \nbecoming the voice of India in his ‘Mann ki Baat ’ on 31 st December, \n2017 and also reiterated his desire to organise the Youth Parliament   \nin his address during inauguration of the 22 nd National Youth Festival \non 12 th January, 2018.  Accordingly, i n the  year 2019, the National \nYouth Festival was merged with Nation al Youth Parliament Festival \nand was organised from 12 th January to 27 thFebruary, 2019 with an \nobjective to hear the voice of youth, to encourage the youth to     \n\nengage with public issues, understand the common man ’s point of \nview, form opinion and express it  in an articulate manner and to \ndevelop and enhance decision making abilities . The National Youth \nParliament Festival was inaugurated by the then Hon’ble MoS(IC) Col. \nRajyavardhan Rathore (Retd.) on 12 th January, 2019. The festival was \nconducted at Nationa l, State and District level wherein about 88,000 \nyouths were heard through walk in and digital screening.  56 finalists \nwere heard by a panel of eminent jury members in final round held on \n26th February, 2019 at Dr. B. R. Ambedkar International Centre, New  \nDelhi in presence of Minister (YA&S) and other dignitaries. \nHon’ble Prime Minister conferred the Award to the 3 winners of \nthe National Youth Parliament Festival on 27 th February, 2019 at \nVigyan Bhawan, New Delhi.  \nThe National Youth Award which is conferred by this Ministry   \non 12th January every year is to be conferred on 12th August, 2019  i.e. \non International Youth Day, this year since these could not be \nawarded on 12th January. \n \n(c) & (d)     At present, there is no proposal under consideration for \nrevamping the entire festival and award nomination system.  \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|1|UNSTARRED |964", "t": "Setting up of MSMEs", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES\n \n \nLOK SABHA\n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 964\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON: 27.06.2019\n \n \nSETTING UP OF MSMEs\n \n \n964.  \n \nSHRI RAMPRIT MANDAL:\n \n \nSHRI DHARAMBIR SINGH:\n \n \nWill the Minister of MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES be pleased to state:\n \n \n(a)\n \nwhether Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs) have been set up in the \ncountry particularly under the MUDRA Yojana in the country during the last three years;\n \n(b)\n \nif so, the total number of such units set up in the country during the year 2016\n-\n17, \n2017\n-\n18 and 2018\n-\n19, State/UT wise; \n \n(c)\n \nthe total value of the business transacted by above units during each of the said year; \nand\n \n(d)   \n \nthe\n \ntotal amount of subsidy released by the Union Government to the State Government \nof Haryana for setting up of MSMEs? \n \n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES\n \n(\nSHRI \n \nNITIN GADKARI\n)\n \n \n(a)\nto(c):\n \nUnder MUDRA Yojana\n,\n \nloans  up to Rs.10 lakh are provided to micro units \nfor no\nn\n \nfarm, income generating activities. \n \nDetails of loan accounts and amount sanctioned \nunder the Scheme in last three financial years as per information on MUDRA portal is given \ni\nn the table below:\n \n \nCategory\n \n2016\n-\n17\n \n2017\n-\n18\n \n2018\n-\n19\n \n \nNo. of \nAccounts\n \nAmount \nsanctioned\n \nNo. of \nAccounts\n \nAmount \nsanctioned\n \nNo. of \nAccounts\n \nAmount \nsanctioned\n \n(lakhs)\n \n(Rs. in \ncrores)\n \n(lakhs)\n \n(Rs. in \ncrores)\n \n(lakhs)\n \n(Rs. in \ncrores)\n \nSHISHU\n \n364.98\n \n85,100.74\n \n426.69\n \n1,06,001.60\n \n515.07\n \n1,42,345.25\n \nKISHORE\n \n26.64\n \n53,545.14\n \n46.53\n \n86,732.16\n \n66.06\n \n1,04,386.68\n \nTARUN\n \n5.39\n \n41,882.66\n \n8.06\n \n60,943.34\n \n17.58\n \n74,990.86\n \nTOTAL\n \n397.01\n \n1,80,528.54\n \n481.28\n \n2,53,677.1\n \n598.71\n \n3,21,722.79\n \n \n(d): \n \nThe margin money subsidy given to \nHaryana under Prime Minister’s Employment \nGeneration Programme for setting up of MSME units\n \nwas Rs.4664.1 lakh in 2018\n-\n19.\n \n \n \n****\n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|1|UNSTARRED |965", "t": "Construction of NH-31", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 965 \nANSWERED ON 27TH JUNE, 2019 \n \nCONSTRUCTION OF NH-31 \n \n965.  MS. ANNPURNA DEVI:  \n \n  Will the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \nसडक़ प\u0001रवहन और राजमाग\u0001 मं\u0001ी \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the construction work of National Highway (NH) No. 31 between Barhi\n (Jharkhand) and Rajauli (Bihar) was started four years back by the National Highways \n Authority of India;  \n(b) if so, whether the construction work  on the said road has not been completed so far; \n and  \n(c)  whether the Government will ensure the construction of the said road in the fixed time \n frame and if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n(SHRI NITIN JAIRAM GADKARI) \n \n(a) to (c) Barhi-Rajauli section of NH -31 has total length of about 47.40 Km.  The project \nstretch has been divided into two packages.  \n \n Package-I i.e. Barhi to Koderma section of NH -31 of length 27.50 km has \nalready been awarded in February, 2019.   \n \n Package-II i.e. Koderma to Rajauli section of length 20.00 km has not been \nawarded in want of requisite pre- construction activities and wild life clearance.  \n \n***** \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|1|UNSTARRED |966", "t": "Solar Energy Plants", "head": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF NEW AND RENEWABLE ENRGY \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 966 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 27.06.2019 \n \nSOLAR ENERGY PLANTS \n \n \n966. SHRI BHANU PRATAP SINGH VERMA \n \n \nWill the Minister of NEW AND RENEWABLE ENERGY be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the number of Solar Energy Plants under construction in Uttar Pradesh at present, district -\nwise; \n \n(b) the details of constructed and under construction plants in Bundelkhand region; and \n \n(c) the quantum of energy targeted to be generated from the construction of these plants?  \n \nANSWER \n \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (I/C) FOR NEW & RENEWABLE ENERGY AND POWER  \n(SHRI R. K. SINGH) \n \n(a) The Government of Uttar Pradesh has reported allocation of 38 nos. of Solar Power Plants of \ncapacity 1435 MW including 385 MW capacity under Open Access for sale of power to third \nparty or for captive use for their commissioning from Marc h to September, 2020. The district -\nwise details are given at Annexure-I. \n \n(b) The details of constructed and under construction plants in Bundelkhand region are given at \nAnnexure-II. \n \n(c) The quantum of energy targeted to be generated from the construction  of these plants has \nbeen reported as 2388.41 MU. \n***** \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \nANNEXURE-I \nANNEXURE-I REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) OF LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 966 FOR 27.06.2019 \n \nDISTRICT-WISE LIST OF SOLAR POWER PLANTS ALLOCATED FOR \nCONSTRUCTION IN UTTAR PRADESH:- \nS. No District Project capacity \n(MW) \nType \n1 Jhansi 2X20 PPA with UPPCL \n2 Kanpur Nagar 140 PPA with UPPCL \n3 Kanpur Nagar 85 PPA with UPPCL \n4 Badau 3x 50 PPA with UPPCL \n5 Jalaun 50 PPA with UPPCL \n6 Jalaun 70 PPA with UPPCL \n7 Shahajahanpur 3 x 50 PPA with UPPCL \n8 Shahajahanpur 2X10 Open Access \nCaptive/Third party sale \n9 Auriya 20 PPA with UPPCL \n10 Chitrakoot 2X 50 PPA with UPPCL \n11 Chitrakoot 25 PPA with UPPCL \n12 Mirzapur 70 PPA with UPPCL \n13 Mirzapur 100 PPA with UPPCL \n14 Mirzapur 50 Open Access \nCaptive/Third party sale \n15 Agra 50 PPA with UPPCL \n16 Bahraich 20 Open Access \nCaptive/Third party sale \n17 Bahraich 10 Open Access Captive/         \nThird party sa