s schemes including \nDeen Dayal Upadhyaya Gram Jyoti Yojana (DDUGJY),  Integrated Power \nDevelopment Scheme (IPDS), Pradhan Mantri Sahaj Bijli Har Ghar Yojana -\nSaubhagya and Ujjwal Discom Assurance Yojana (UDAY).   Urban area s are \nexpected to have regular supply.  Urban area covered under RAPDRP are reported \non Urja App to have average outage hours as given at Annexure-I.  The State-wise \naverage number of hours of power supply to rural areas, is given in Annexure-II.   \n************** \n \n \n \n \n\n \nANNEXURE-I \n \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (d) OF UNSTARRED \nQUESTION NO.  992 TO BE ANSWERED IN THE LOK SABHA ON 27.06.2019. \n*************** \n  \nState-wise  monthly Average Duration of Power Cuts in Urban area \n(RAPDRP) at 11KV feeder level \n  May, 2019 \nSl. No Name Value \n1 Jammu & Kashmir 0:24 hrs \n2 Rajasthan 0:26 hrs \n3 Gujarat 1:07 hrs \n4 Kerala 1:31 hrs \n5 Andhra Pradesh 1:58 hrs \n6 Maharashtra 2:16 hrs \n7 Telangana 2:33 hrs \n8 Uttar Pradesh 2:48 hrs \n9 Tripura 3:10 hrs \n10 Madhya Pradesh 4:10 hrs \n11 Himachal Pradesh 5:16 hrs \n12 Goa 6:55 hrs \n13 West Bengal 8:37 hrs \n14 Karnataka 9:34 hrs \n15 Punjab 10:16 hrs \n16 Uttarakhand 14:05 hrs \n17 Chhattisgarh 17:17 hrs \n18 Haryana 18:37 hrs \n19 Manipur 25:43 hrs \n      \n \n**************** \n  \n\n \n \nANNEXURE-II \n \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (d) OF UNSTARRED \nQUESTION NO.  992 TO BE ANSWERED IN THE LOK SABHA ON 27.06.2019. \n*************** \n \nStatus of Power Supply to Rural Areas \n  \nApril, 2019 \nSL. No.  State Average power supply in a day \n1 Andhra Pradesh 23.90 \n2 Arunachal Pradesh* 14.30 \n3 Assam 19.00 \n4 Bihar 22.07 \n5 Chhattisgarh 23.00 \n6 Gujarat 24.00 \n7 Haryana 15.64 \n8 Himachal Pradesh 24.00 \n9 Jammu & Kashmir 14.25 \n10 Jharkhand  17.71 \n11 Karnataka 18.74 \n12 Kerala 24.00 \n13 Madhya Pradesh 23.63 \n14 Maharashtra 24.00 \n15 Manipur  22.50 \n16 Meghalaya 18.50 \n17 Mizoram 15.00 \n18 Nagaland 20.00 \n19 Odisha 20.69 \n20 Punjab 24.00 \n21 Rajasthan 22.00 \n22 Sikkim 17.13 \n23 Tamil Nadu 24.00 \n24 Telangana 24.00 \n25 Tripura 23.50 \n26 Uttar Pradesh* 17.89 \n27 Uttarakhand 23.60 \n28 West Bengal  24.00 \n* for Arunachal Pradesh & Uttar Pradesh March 2019 data. \n \n************** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|1|UNSTARRED |993", "t": "Public Transport Vehicle", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 993 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON JUNE 27, 2019 \n \nPUBLIC TRANSPORT VEHICLE \nNo. 993 SHRI KUNWAR PUSHPENDRA SINGH CHANDEL.  \n \nWill the Minister of HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS be pleased to \nstate: \n \n \na) whether the Government proposes to run major mea ns of public \ntransport vehicle at a very low prices in tier-2 an dtier-3 category \ncities; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n \n(c) whether the Government has taken initiative to cooperate with \nprivate sectors for this purpose; and \n \n(d) if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) OF THE \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \n(SHRI HARDEEP SINGH PURI) \n(a) to (d) Urban Transport is intertwined with Urba n Development, \nwhich is a State subject.  As such the initiatives to provide public \ntransport in tier-2 and tier- 3 categorycities andt he scope of \ncooperation with private sectors for this purpose a re taken up by \nthe State Governments / Union Territories/Urban Local Bodies.  \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|1|UNSTARRED |994", "t": "Disabled and Elderly Accessible Government Buildings", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 994 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON JUNE 27, 2019. \n \nDISABLED AND ELDERLY ACCESSIBLE GOVERNMENT BUILDINGS \nNO. 994 DR. SHASHI THAROOR : \nWill the Minister of HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS be p leased \nto state: \n(a) Whether the Government’s 2015 guidelines to mak e all the \nGovernment buildings accessible to disabled and eld erly have \nbeen implemented; \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n(c) if not, the reasons therefor; and \n(d) the number of the Government buildings that hav e been made \naccessible after the formulation of the guidelines.  State/UT-\nwise? \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) OF THE \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS  \n(SHRI HARDEEP SINGH PURI) \n(a) to (d): The guidelines relating to making Gover nment buildings \naccessible to disabled and elderly have been adopte d for \nimplementation.  Central Public Works Department ha ve made \n811 Central Government buildings in different state s/UTs \nunder its maintenance, accessible to disabled and e lderly.  \nState/UT wise details are attached as ‘Annexure A’.    \n***** \n\nAnnexure ‘A’  \n \nDetails of State/UT wise Government Buildings under maintenance \nof Central Public Works Department made accessible to disabled \nand elderly referred in reply to Part (a) to (d) of Lok Sabha Unstarred \nQuestion No. 994 for 27 th  June, 2019.  \n \nSl. No. State No. of Buildings \n1. Andhra Pradesh and Telangana 39 \n2. Andaman & Nicobar 09 \n3. Bihar 15 \n4. Chhattisgarh 05 \n5. Delhi 165 \n6. Gujarat 40 \n7. Goa 07 \n8. Himachal Pradesh 24 \n9. Jharkhand 16 \n10. Jammu & Kashmir 03 \n11. Karnataka 26 \n12. Kerala 19 \n13. Madhya Pradesh 62 \n14. Maharashtra 91 \n15. North East States 56 \n16. Odisha 17 \n17. Punjab & Haryana 20 \n18. Puducherry 04 \n19. Port Blair 02 \n20. Rajasthan 52 \n21. Sikkim 04 \n22. Tamilnadu 46 \n23. Uttar Pradesh 30 \n24. Uttarakhand 10 \n25. West Bengal 49 \n TOTAL 811 \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|1|UNSTARRED |995", "t": "Reconstruction of Roads in Kerala", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS  \n \nLOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 995 \nANSWERED ON 27TH JUNE, 2019 \n \nRECONSTRUCTION OF ROADS IN KERALA \n \n995.  SHRI ANTO ANTONY \n \nWill the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \nसड़क परिवहन औि िाजमार्ग मंत्री \nbe pleased to state: \n (a)  whether the Union Government  has received any request from the State  \nGovernment of Kerala for financial  assistance for reconstruction of roads  damaged \ndue to recent flood in that State; \n(b)  if so, the details thereof and the response of the Union Government in this regard; \n(c)  whether the Union Government  has any statistics regarding financial  assistance \ngiven to various States for  construction/development of roads and  if so, the details \nof such assistance during each of the last five years, State-wise; and \n(d)  whether the Union Government  has any plan to give more financial  assistance to \nKerala for reconstruction and improvement of roads and if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n(SHRI NITIN JAIRAM GADKARI) \n (a)&(b) This Ministry is primarily responsible for development and maintenance of \nNational Highways (NHs) in the country.  This Ministry has not received any \nspecific request for financial assistance for reconstruction  of roads damaged due to \nrecent floods in Kerala.  For maintenance of various NHs in Kerala including those \ndamaged by 2018 floods, this Ministry allocated Rs. 121.10 crore to the  Kerala \nState PWD. Besides, strengthening works in 123 km of various National Highways \nin Kerala were sanctioned for Rs. 188.53 Crore during 2018-19.   \n(c)&(d) State-wise and year -wise financial allocation given by this Ministry to various \nStates for development of NHs during last five years is enclosed as Annexure-I and \nfor development of State roads  under Central Road Fund (CRF)  Scheme, now \nCentral Road Infrastructure Fund (CRIF)  during the same period is enclosed as \nAnnexure-II.   \n  \n  \n\nANNEXURE -I \nANNEXURE-I REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (c) & (d) OF LOK SABHA UNSTARRED \nQUESTION NO. 995 FOR ANSWER ON 27TH JUNE, 2019 ASKED BY SHRI ANTO ANTONY \nREGARDING RECONSTRUCTION OF ROADS IN KERALA  \nFinancial Allocation to various